WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.920 --> 00:00:05.839
I wish I had gone with my instinct

00:00:05.840 --> 00:00:07.639
the first time I injected heroin.

00:00:13.030 --> 00:00:14.710
I would tell myself, "Leave it."

00:00:22.310 --> 00:00:24.289
I've hit 20,000 rock bottoms.

00:00:24.290 --> 00:00:25.850
I have been as low as you

00:00:27.110 --> 00:00:28.699
can go, and you can't go any

00:00:28.700 --> 00:00:29.700
further.

00:00:31.800 --> 00:00:33.629
I don't want to be that

00:00:33.630 --> 00:00:35.130
example for my daughter.

00:00:39.380 --> 00:00:41.630
I can't be dead on my bathroom floor

00:00:43.340 --> 00:00:44.630
because that's not fair to her.

00:00:48.220 --> 00:00:50.229
In 2020, Serene, who

00:00:50.230 --> 00:00:52.239
asked that we not use her last name,

00:00:52.240 --> 00:00:53.859
reached out to two brothers named

00:00:53.860 --> 00:00:55.607
Rory and Ryan Van Tuinen.

00:00:56.620 --> 00:00:57.639
Hi.

00:00:57.640 --> 00:00:59.589
Based in Waterbury, Vermont, they

00:00:59.590 --> 00:01:01.329
had started a nonprofit with the

00:01:01.330 --> 00:01:03.189
goal of building a community that

00:01:03.190 --> 00:01:04.809
can help people to overcome

00:01:04.810 --> 00:01:06.939
addiction and improve their mental

00:01:06.940 --> 00:01:07.959
health.

00:01:07.960 --> 00:01:09.789
I contacted Rory and

00:01:09.790 --> 00:01:11.739
Ryan as I had seen an

00:01:11.740 --> 00:01:14.739
article called Cultivating

00:01:14.740 --> 00:01:16.569
Connections, and I had

00:01:16.570 --> 00:01:18.369
read both their stories.

00:01:18.370 --> 00:01:20.199
Rory had taken the psychedelic drug

00:01:20.200 --> 00:01:22.479
ayahuasca in 2019,

00:01:22.480 --> 00:01:24.249
which was a last ditch attempt to

00:01:24.250 --> 00:01:26.529
overcome a ten-year heroin addiction

00:01:26.530 --> 00:01:28.509
that had derailed his life.

00:01:28.510 --> 00:01:30.249
"Neither Ryan nor Rory believe that

00:01:30.250 --> 00:01:32.199
hallucinogens are a cure-all."

00:01:32.200 --> 00:01:34.089
But "without the ayahuasca,"

00:01:34.090 --> 00:01:35.949
he'd either "still be using" or

00:01:35.950 --> 00:01:37.959
he'd "be dead." The key was

00:01:37.960 --> 00:01:39.429
to accompany the drug "with the

00:01:39.430 --> 00:01:41.349
cultivation of meaningful human

00:01:41.350 --> 00:01:42.350
relationships."

00:01:52.450 --> 00:01:54.369
I'm at such a weak point because

00:01:54.370 --> 00:01:55.449
I'm in so much pain.

00:01:56.500 --> 00:01:58.389
Not so much, I mean, physical and

00:01:58.390 --> 00:01:59.409
mental pain.

00:01:59.410 --> 00:02:00.699
I really want to help.

00:02:00.700 --> 00:02:02.049
Like, I don't, I don't know what I

00:02:02.050 --> 00:02:03.009
can even help.

00:02:03.010 --> 00:02:03.939
I don't know.

00:02:03.940 --> 00:02:05.949
But I want to, you know, I have

00:02:05.950 --> 00:02:06.950
that urge and...

00:02:11.130 --> 00:02:12.130
Yes.

00:02:21.750 --> 00:02:23.579
Psychologist Andrew Tatarsky is the

00:02:23.580 --> 00:02:25.379
founder and director of the Center

00:02:25.380 --> 00:02:27.899
for Optimal Living in New York City,

00:02:27.900 --> 00:02:29.879
and he specializes in addiction

00:02:29.880 --> 00:02:32.069
and harm reduction therapy.

00:02:32.070 --> 00:02:33.989
What are the promises of

00:02:33.990 --> 00:02:35.849
psychedelics when it comes

00:02:35.850 --> 00:02:37.979
to treating things like addiction?

00:02:37.980 --> 00:02:40.349
Our core beliefs, our behaviors,

00:02:40.350 --> 00:02:42.239
our patterns of relating, our

00:02:42.240 --> 00:02:44.759
patterns of coping get encoded

00:02:44.760 --> 00:02:46.619
in neural networks, which is

00:02:46.620 --> 00:02:48.539
why they're so difficult to

00:02:48.540 --> 00:02:50.819
change. Psychedelic substances

00:02:50.820 --> 00:02:52.799
have this really interesting and

00:02:52.800 --> 00:02:54.629
unique capacity to

00:02:54.630 --> 00:02:56.819
loosen those structures,

00:02:56.820 --> 00:02:58.649
in some cases dissolve

00:02:58.650 --> 00:03:00.689
them so that people

00:03:00.690 --> 00:03:02.969
have the opportunity to

00:03:02.970 --> 00:03:05.099
kind of rework their relationship

00:03:05.100 --> 00:03:06.989
to themselves and the world and

00:03:06.990 --> 00:03:08.849
develop new structures that

00:03:08.850 --> 00:03:10.619
are more adaptive, more effective.

00:03:13.900 --> 00:03:15.639
Rory and Ryan have not asked for

00:03:15.640 --> 00:03:17.499
money for endorsements.

00:03:17.500 --> 00:03:18.689
They expect nothing from.

00:03:33.730 --> 00:03:35.439
I hope the ayahuasca will help me

00:03:35.440 --> 00:03:37.270
find my center of self again.

00:03:40.840 --> 00:03:42.789
But Tatarsky also warns that this

00:03:42.790 --> 00:03:44.709
powerful tool is creating

00:03:44.710 --> 00:03:46.599
new problems for some people

00:03:46.600 --> 00:03:48.579
suffering from addiction or mental

00:03:48.580 --> 00:03:49.509
illness.

00:03:49.510 --> 00:03:51.219
When administered by untrained

00:03:51.220 --> 00:03:53.109
practitioners, these drugs

00:03:53.110 --> 00:03:54.710
can do more harm than good.

00:03:55.900 --> 00:03:58.839
If you face a traumatic experience

00:03:58.840 --> 00:04:00.669
and it is overwhelming to you

00:04:00.670 --> 00:04:01.749
and you don't have the kind of

00:04:01.750 --> 00:04:03.579
support to be able to

00:04:03.580 --> 00:04:05.799
titrate and kind of

00:04:05.800 --> 00:04:08.079
manage the emotional intensity

00:04:08.080 --> 00:04:10.269
that comes up, it can actually

00:04:10.270 --> 00:04:12.069
be itself another traumatic

00:04:12.070 --> 00:04:13.059
experience.

00:04:13.060 --> 00:04:14.889
But also, one of the ways

00:04:14.890 --> 00:04:16.599
that people deal with overwhelming

00:04:16.600 --> 00:04:18.489
emotional experiences is

00:04:18.490 --> 00:04:20.469
by becoming psychotic.

00:04:20.470 --> 00:04:22.599
And we've had a number

00:04:22.600 --> 00:04:24.729
of people coming to our,

00:04:24.730 --> 00:04:26.739
to us for therapy

00:04:26.740 --> 00:04:28.659
following a series of psychedelic

00:04:28.660 --> 00:04:30.729
experiences that left them

00:04:30.730 --> 00:04:32.649
completely paranoid and psychotic.

00:04:37.380 --> 00:04:38.490
How do you guys feel about doing the

00:04:38.491 --> 00:04:40.259
ceremony next week?

00:04:42.090 --> 00:04:43.379
Yeah, sure.

00:04:56.410 --> 00:04:58.149
So I came to learn about psychedelic

00:04:58.150 --> 00:05:00.279
medicine when I was 23

00:05:00.280 --> 00:05:02.319
and had my first experience.

00:05:02.320 --> 00:05:03.249
That really helped me with

00:05:03.250 --> 00:05:04.250
depression.

00:05:07.160 --> 00:05:09.169
In the following years, I saw Rory

00:05:09.170 --> 00:05:10.879
really struggling with addiction,

00:05:10.880 --> 00:05:12.709
and so I talked to Rory about

00:05:13.760 --> 00:05:14.760
ayahuasca and psilocybin.

00:05:17.870 --> 00:05:18.870
After the ayahuasca, I'd

00:05:19.820 --> 00:05:21.829
stayed clean from opiates for 13 to

00:05:21.830 --> 00:05:23.869
14 months, which was

00:05:23.870 --> 00:05:25.849
by far the longest

00:05:25.850 --> 00:05:27.829
clean time I'd ever had.

00:05:30.410 --> 00:05:32.479
When your child has a

00:05:32.480 --> 00:05:33.709
bad opioid addiction,

00:05:34.850 --> 00:05:36.559
it wears you out and eventually you

00:05:36.560 --> 00:05:38.839
realize you got,

00:05:38.840 --> 00:05:40.009
you can't be attached to the

00:05:40.010 --> 00:05:41.010
outcome.

00:05:45.760 --> 00:05:48.099
You know, Rory's struggled with

00:05:48.100 --> 00:05:50.079
addiction issues for a long,

00:05:50.080 --> 00:05:51.080
long time.

00:05:52.510 --> 00:05:53.979
He had tried rehab a number of

00:05:53.980 --> 00:05:55.839
times, and he had

00:05:55.840 --> 00:05:57.879
overdosed a number of times,

00:05:57.880 --> 00:05:59.829
and he wasn't seeing any way out.

00:06:01.780 --> 00:06:03.610
It's clear that that ayahuasca has

00:06:05.170 --> 00:06:07.779
led to some real changes

00:06:07.780 --> 00:06:10.419
in his ability to control

00:06:10.420 --> 00:06:12.519
his addiction to the

00:06:12.520 --> 00:06:13.520
opioids.

00:06:27.990 --> 00:06:29.909
My main goal is to not have to be

00:06:29.910 --> 00:06:31.739
on anything so I can be a better

00:06:31.740 --> 00:06:32.740
mother for her.

00:06:35.480 --> 00:06:37.699
Lily is the most important

00:06:37.700 --> 00:06:39.499
person in my life, even above

00:06:39.500 --> 00:06:40.500
myself.

00:06:41.180 --> 00:06:43.309
If I did not have Lily, I wouldn't

00:06:43.310 --> 00:06:44.310
bother.

00:06:51.140 --> 00:06:52.250
I don't know how to get better.

00:06:53.600 --> 00:06:55.069
You you know I've tried, you know

00:06:55.070 --> 00:06:55.849
I've been...

00:06:55.850 --> 00:06:56.659
You're doing the steps to get

00:06:56.660 --> 00:06:57.979
better, you know.

00:06:57.980 --> 00:06:59.089
You know how to get better.

00:06:59.090 --> 00:07:00.349
You're doing it.

00:07:00.350 --> 00:07:01.789
You're walking the path to get

00:07:01.790 --> 00:07:02.449
better.

00:07:02.450 --> 00:07:04.669
Yeah, but using it's still not...but

00:07:04.670 --> 00:07:05.869
the methadone is clearly not helping

00:07:05.870 --> 00:07:07.309
if that's, you know, I mean, like...

00:07:08.390 --> 00:07:10.169
It's not helping keep me sober.

00:07:10.170 --> 00:07:12.079
It's not helping with pain.

00:07:16.070 --> 00:07:18.289
I gotta to say almost every dealer

00:07:18.290 --> 00:07:20.149
I've met around here was through the

00:07:20.150 --> 00:07:21.150
methadone clinic.

00:07:22.750 --> 00:07:25.149
The wonderful thing about methadone

00:07:25.150 --> 00:07:26.979
and similar substances,

00:07:26.980 --> 00:07:29.109
buprenorphine, is that

00:07:29.110 --> 00:07:31.269
if there is a physiological

00:07:31.270 --> 00:07:33.159
depletion in a certain

00:07:33.160 --> 00:07:35.199
brain substance that leads

00:07:35.200 --> 00:07:37.149
people to need a drug in order

00:07:37.150 --> 00:07:39.039
to stabilize and feel

00:07:39.040 --> 00:07:40.989
normal, if you can replace that

00:07:40.990 --> 00:07:42.699
with another drug that actually

00:07:42.700 --> 00:07:45.069
meets that physical need,

00:07:45.070 --> 00:07:46.809
you can actually help stabilize

00:07:46.810 --> 00:07:48.339
somebody medically.

00:07:48.340 --> 00:07:50.859
Medication assisted treatment

00:07:50.860 --> 00:07:52.689
doesn't address the

00:07:52.690 --> 00:07:54.789
complex, emotional,

00:07:54.790 --> 00:07:57.279
relational, you know,

00:07:57.280 --> 00:07:59.379
psychological factors

00:07:59.380 --> 00:08:01.299
that may be expressed in

00:08:01.300 --> 00:08:03.099
that addictive process.

00:08:03.100 --> 00:08:05.349
And here's where psychedelics

00:08:05.350 --> 00:08:07.899
can really powerfully facilitate

00:08:07.900 --> 00:08:08.900
those insights.

00:08:16.920 --> 00:08:19.019
I think this ayahuasca experience

00:08:19.020 --> 00:08:20.909
can help open Serene up

00:08:20.910 --> 00:08:22.993
to the possibilities for the future.

00:08:27.040 --> 00:08:28.040
Serene. Hey.

00:08:31.830 --> 00:08:33.779
The way I envision coming out

00:08:33.780 --> 00:08:34.782
on the other side is like, like

00:08:37.830 --> 00:08:39.719
caterpillars turn into the

00:08:39.720 --> 00:08:41.009
pupa and then come out the

00:08:41.010 --> 00:08:42.010
butterfly.

00:08:51.950 --> 00:08:53.779
One of the dangers is

00:08:53.780 --> 00:08:56.449
that people go into the experience

00:08:56.450 --> 00:08:59.659
with unrealistic expectations

00:08:59.660 --> 00:09:00.660
for a cure.

00:09:02.180 --> 00:09:04.309
And I think this is a big problem

00:09:04.310 --> 00:09:05.989
because of all of the hype about

00:09:05.990 --> 00:09:07.999
psychedelics and go through

00:09:08.000 --> 00:09:09.173
the experience feeling

00:09:10.250 --> 00:09:11.250
no cure

00:09:12.290 --> 00:09:13.789
and maybe feeling worse

00:09:15.230 --> 00:09:16.459
and that that can really

00:09:16.460 --> 00:09:19.519
precipitate, you know, profound

00:09:19.520 --> 00:09:20.591
depressions and suicidality.

00:09:21.830 --> 00:09:24.259
So proper preparation,

00:09:24.260 --> 00:09:26.809
you know, measured expectations

00:09:26.810 --> 00:09:29.479
or even no expectations,

00:09:29.480 --> 00:09:31.699
that is to go into the experience

00:09:31.700 --> 00:09:34.039
as an experience that,

00:09:34.040 --> 00:09:36.259
you know, you know, discover what

00:09:36.260 --> 00:09:37.260
it will be like.

00:09:43.430 --> 00:09:44.569
You're going to have this sleeping

00:09:44.570 --> 00:09:45.169
bag?

00:09:45.170 --> 00:09:45.619
Sure.

00:09:45.620 --> 00:09:46.561
I'll be here, Rory there.

00:09:46.562 --> 00:09:46.609
OK

00:09:46.610 --> 00:09:47.610
Thank you.

00:09:54.330 --> 00:09:56.609
I don't know, how much I should say,

00:09:56.610 --> 00:09:57.610
but I can see it in you.

00:10:02.350 --> 00:10:03.350
Glad to be here.

00:10:09.000 --> 00:10:10.000
Delish.

00:10:11.850 --> 00:10:11.883
It's a bit astringent, eh.

00:10:11.884 --> 00:10:12.884
...throw up

00:10:24.700 --> 00:10:25.700
Oh.

00:10:39.010 --> 00:10:40.010
Thank you.

00:10:42.610 --> 00:10:43.610
Mm hmm.

00:10:50.130 --> 00:10:51.130
It's all you, girl.

00:11:06.420 --> 00:11:06.879
Thank you so much.

00:11:06.880 --> 00:11:07.880
Thank you.

00:11:28.850 --> 00:11:30.709
When you look at that scene, how do

00:11:30.710 --> 00:11:33.590
you respond as a psychotherapist?

00:11:34.940 --> 00:11:36.470
My sense is that,

00:11:37.880 --> 00:11:39.049
you know, they are

00:11:40.370 --> 00:11:42.368
very, very well-meaning,

00:11:44.480 --> 00:11:46.639
kind, supportive,

00:11:46.640 --> 00:11:48.469
caring, seem to

00:11:48.470 --> 00:11:50.299
have had their own experiences that

00:11:50.300 --> 00:11:52.249
were very positive and

00:11:52.250 --> 00:11:54.139
they wanted to pass this on

00:11:54.140 --> 00:11:56.479
and share this with Serene.

00:11:56.480 --> 00:11:58.669
But these guys

00:11:58.670 --> 00:12:00.409
are not therapists.

00:12:00.410 --> 00:12:02.089
I don't believe that they have any

00:12:02.090 --> 00:12:04.339
training or any capability

00:12:04.340 --> 00:12:06.319
of dealing with, you know,

00:12:06.320 --> 00:12:09.259
serious, the emergence of serious,

00:12:09.260 --> 00:12:11.359
painful experiences

00:12:11.360 --> 00:12:12.979
that could be overwhelming,

00:12:12.980 --> 00:12:15.019
retraumatizing and could even

00:12:15.020 --> 00:12:16.909
manifest in a psychotic kind of

00:12:16.910 --> 00:12:17.910
experience

00:12:19.490 --> 00:12:20.490
and

00:12:21.590 --> 00:12:23.089
really dangerous behavior.

00:12:23.090 --> 00:12:24.889
So they are completely unequipped to

00:12:24.890 --> 00:12:26.869
do that, A, B,

00:12:26.870 --> 00:12:29.119
they were also taking the substance.

00:12:29.120 --> 00:12:31.399
A lot of people will not say

00:12:31.400 --> 00:12:33.559
these, these are powerful substances

00:12:33.560 --> 00:12:35.479
with negative potential,

00:12:35.480 --> 00:12:37.369
so they should be banned, but

00:12:37.370 --> 00:12:39.199
rather they should be heavily

00:12:39.200 --> 00:12:41.119
restricted to a

00:12:41.120 --> 00:12:43.459
class of therapists or doctors

00:12:43.460 --> 00:12:45.469
or authorities

00:12:45.470 --> 00:12:46.820
who know what they're doing.

00:12:49.160 --> 00:12:50.989
What do you think about that?

00:12:50.990 --> 00:12:54.229
As a psychotherapist

00:12:54.230 --> 00:12:56.719
and as a psychedelic

00:12:56.720 --> 00:12:58.010
assisted therapist?

00:13:00.170 --> 00:13:02.299
I believe that psychedelic assisted

00:13:02.300 --> 00:13:04.429
therapy should be performed by

00:13:04.430 --> 00:13:06.380
very well trained therapists.

00:13:07.460 --> 00:13:09.614
So, you know, they weren't equipped,

00:13:10.640 --> 00:13:12.649
they're not professionally trained,

00:13:12.650 --> 00:13:14.929
they were themselves intoxicated.

00:13:14.930 --> 00:13:16.909
But prohibition only

00:13:16.910 --> 00:13:18.619
creates problems for people.

00:13:18.620 --> 00:13:20.239
People are going to use drugs if

00:13:20.240 --> 00:13:21.949
they want to use drugs, they'll find

00:13:21.950 --> 00:13:23.149
them on the internet, they'll find

00:13:23.150 --> 00:13:24.379
them in the park, they'll find them

00:13:24.380 --> 00:13:25.969
with their friends.

00:13:25.970 --> 00:13:27.889
So the more help

00:13:27.890 --> 00:13:30.169
and support and information

00:13:30.170 --> 00:13:31.789
we can make available to people, the

00:13:31.790 --> 00:13:33.589
more we can reduce the risks

00:13:33.590 --> 00:13:34.640
associated with that.

00:13:58.840 --> 00:14:00.009
Me and Rory got kind of lucky with

00:14:00.010 --> 00:14:00.999
it.

00:14:01.000 --> 00:14:02.229
The experience that we had and then

00:14:02.230 --> 00:14:04.239
we try to recreate that for someone

00:14:04.240 --> 00:14:06.369
else. And it's,

00:14:06.370 --> 00:14:08.349
it's not really, you know, just

00:14:08.350 --> 00:14:09.639
a simple process.

00:14:27.190 --> 00:14:29.679
Are you surprised to learn

00:14:29.680 --> 00:14:32.049
that after this experience Serene

00:14:32.050 --> 00:14:33.940
went back to using heroin?

00:14:36.370 --> 00:14:37.720
No, not at all.

00:14:38.950 --> 00:14:40.779
Reworking your relationship to

00:14:40.780 --> 00:14:42.699
that substance means

00:14:42.700 --> 00:14:44.739
understanding the relationship,

00:14:44.740 --> 00:14:46.719
really making the connection between

00:14:46.720 --> 00:14:48.699
that substance and what function

00:14:48.700 --> 00:14:50.139
and meaning it's playing in your

00:14:50.140 --> 00:14:50.949
life.

00:14:50.950 --> 00:14:52.959
And gradually over time, kind

00:14:52.960 --> 00:14:53.960
of letting go.

00:14:59.700 --> 00:15:02.189
These are very, very exciting

00:15:02.190 --> 00:15:04.229
times when

00:15:04.230 --> 00:15:06.629
growing body of research

00:15:06.630 --> 00:15:08.609
change the way that we

00:15:08.610 --> 00:15:11.129
both look at psychedelics,

00:15:11.130 --> 00:15:12.690
viewing them as potential

00:15:14.220 --> 00:15:16.049
wonderful tools that

00:15:16.050 --> 00:15:18.029
we can use for the benefit

00:15:18.030 --> 00:15:20.039
of humans in many different

00:15:20.040 --> 00:15:21.179
